(The resistance of a constantan wire) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Introduction) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Electrical resistance describes how strongly a component opposes the current through it.) Tj T*
(For a uniform wire, R = rhoL/A, where rho is the resistivity of the material, L the length and) Tj T*
(A the cross-sectional area. If the temperature of the wire stays constant, the resistance) Tj T*
(should be directly proportional to the length, so a graph of R against L should be a) Tj T*
(straight line through the origin with gradient rho/A. Constantan is used because its) Tj T*
(resistivity changes very little with temperature.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Research question: How does the resistance of a 0.38 mm diameter constantan wire depend on) Tj T*
(its length between 0.10 m and 0.90 m at room temperature?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Hypothesis) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I predict that resistance is directly proportional to length, because each additional) Tj T*
(section of wire adds the same opposition to the current.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Variables) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The independent variable is the length of wire between the crocodile clips, measured with) Tj T*
(a metre rule. The dependent variable is the resistance, calculated from the potential) Tj T*
(difference across the wire divided by the current through it. The current is kept below) Tj T*
(0.30 A by using a fixed supply voltage of 1.5 V and a protective resistor, so that the) Tj T*
(wire does not heat up noticeably. The same piece of wire is used throughout so that the) Tj T*
(diameter and material do not change.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Method) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The wire was taped along a metre rule. A digital ammeter \(resolution 0.001 A\) was) Tj T*
(connected in series and a digital voltmeter \(resolution 0.01 V\) in parallel with the) Tj T*
(section of wire between the clips. For each length the switch was closed for less than) Tj T*
(five seconds, the readings were recorded and the switch was opened again. Nine lengths) Tj T*
(from 0.10 m to 0.90 m were used, and each was measured three times, moving the clips off) Tj T*
ET
